# Your devices: pairing Derp on a phone with this computer.

derp-devices-title = Your devices
derp-devices-intro = Pair Derp on your phone, and your bookmarks, passwords and open tabs follow you between them.
derp-devices-private = It’s all encrypted on your devices, with a key only they have. Derp’s relay passes it along without being able to read it, and there’s still no account.
derp-devices-pair = Pair a phone
derp-devices-pair-another = Pair another phone
derp-devices-making = Making a pairing code…
derp-devices-qr =
    .aria-label = Pairing code. Point your phone’s camera at it.
derp-devices-step-install = Get Derp for Android on your phone.
derp-devices-step-scan = Point your phone’s camera at this code.
derp-devices-step-open = Open the link in Derp, and tap Pair.
derp-devices-waiting = Waiting for your phone…
derp-devices-cancel = Done
# $name: the device that just paired, like "Derp on a Pixel 8"
derp-devices-paired = Paired with { $name }!
derp-devices-alone = No other devices yet. Pair your phone, and its open tabs show up here.
# $when: how long ago, like "5 minutes ago"
derp-devices-seen = Synced { $when }
derp-devices-no-tabs = No open tabs.
# $problem: what went wrong, like "relay 503"
derp-devices-problem = Couldn’t sync just now ({ $problem }). Derp tries again in a few minutes.
derp-devices-leave = Stop syncing
derp-devices-sync = Sync now
derp-devices-leave-title = Stop syncing?
derp-devices-leave-message = This computer leaves the pair. Its bookmarks and passwords stay here, and your other devices keep theirs. To pair again, you’ll scan a new code.
